# FINAL REVIEW

**Evidence stage: all quantitative evidence is `sim`.** There are no `real` results: no arm, no phone videos, and no supervised session has been run. Numbers below are generated from `results/` and checked by `bench/check_claims.py`.

## 1 Answer to the research question (sim stage)

| Part of the question | Answer | Strength |
|---|---|---|
| ~10 phone videos, no teleop, vs teleop at equal human time | **Video wins in the twin**: {{m4.video_10.all}} vs {{m4.teleop_1x.all}} ({{m4.diff.video10_teleop1x}}). Teleop with its best validated configuration (corrective augmentation): {{m4aug.teleop_1x_aug.all}}. Teleop needed more than 4× the time and still did not catch up: {{m4.teleop_4x.all}} plain, {{m4aug.teleop_4x_aug.all}} augmented. | Strong *in sim*. It depends on the simulated operator model and simplified grasping, so it can flip on real hardware. |
| Minutes of self-practice | One round changed success by {{m4.diff.video_practice_video_10}} at about 4× the human time (supervision + resets) | Negative / not cost-effective as implemented |
| Uncertainty-driven vs random demo requests | {{m5.verdict}} Pooled over rounds 1–5: {{m5.diff.pooled.uncertainty_random}} vs random, {{m5.diff.pooled.uncertainty_round_robin}} vs round-robin | {{m5.strength}} |
| Failure detection + recovery | {{m6.no_recovery}} → {{m6.recovery}} ({{m6.diff.recovery}}); blind retry {{m6.blind_retry_once}}; oracle {{m6.oracle_recovery}} | Moderate–strong in sim; the detector features are all robot-observable |

**Overall: mixed.** Contribution 1 (learning from video) and Contribution 3 (recovery) are supported in simulation. Contribution 2 (uncertainty-driven requests) is {{m5.short}} in its current form.

## 2 Strongest and weakest claims

**Strongest.** (a) Embodiment-aware retargeting with object-centric targets is necessary: raw hand trajectories give {{m4.video_raw.all}} and hand-only targets {{m4.video_hand.all}}, vs {{m4.video_10.all}}. (b) The delta-chunk + temporal-ensembling failure, and its fix with spatial-target chunks: validation items placed went from {{dev.video_10|delta_rel}} to {{dev.video_10|cumulative_minimal (default)}}. This is a general pitfall for anyone running ACT with end-effector deltas on a lagging low-cost arm. (c) Detector-gated retry beats both no retry and blind retry.

**Weakest.** (a) The size of the video-vs-teleop gap, because the teleoperator is a model (speed {{const.operator_speed}} of the robot limit, tracking noise, hesitation). A practised real operator could narrow it. (b) Every perception number, because the hand estimator is ground truth plus Gaussian noise, and the real-world fallback (fingertip caps) is weak ({{m3.sweep.fingertip_caps.f1}} event F1). (c) Generalization numbers, which use a colour-segmentation perceiver that is easier than real clutter.

